# DSMLP job configuration for the E-STEER proof-of-concept.
#
# Copy this file to dsmlp.env (NOT tracked by git -- see ../../.gitignore)
# and fill in the values marked "FILL IN". Everything else is a reasonable
# default sized for this project (a 0.5B model, ~60 short generations) and
# can be left as-is or adjusted.
#
# Source: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/ (launch.sh reference, job modes &
# limits, GPU classes, workspaces & storage). See README.md in this folder
# for the full explanation and citations for every value below.

# --- FILL IN: account- and workspace-specific values ---------------------

# Your DSMLP / UCSD AD username (used to ssh to the login node).
DSMLP_USERNAME=FILL_IN_YOUR_USERNAME

# Absolute path to this project AS SEEN INSIDE THE JOB CONTAINER (not the
# login node). If you rsync the folder to `~` on dsmlp-login, it appears in
# the container as /home/<username>/private/E-steer_2026 -- a plain `~` on
# the login node is mounted as private/ in containers. For a workspace home
# instead, use the path form shown by `workspace -l` on the login node.
# Docs: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/workspaces-and-storage/moving-and-sharing-data/
PROJECT_DIR_ON_DSMLP=FILL_IN_/home/FILL_IN_YOUR_USERNAME/private/E-steer_2026

# --- Defaults you can adjust but don't have to -----------------------------

# GPU class: extra-small (~6GB), small (~12GB, RTX 2080Ti), medium (~24GB),
# large (~48GB), extra-large (~96GB). "small" comfortably fits this 0.5B
# model; raise it only if you intentionally scale the model up.
# Docs: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/gpu-access/gpu-classes/
GPU_CLASS=small

# CPU cores / RAM (GB) / GPU count for the job.
CPUS=4
MEM_GB=16
GPUS=1

# Where steer.py/report.py write results.json, the plots, and SUMMARY.md on
# DSMLP. Defaults to a `results/` subfolder under the project so it never
# collides with (or overwrites) the local-run results already committed at
# the top of this folder. This path is git-ignored.
OUT_DIR=${PROJECT_DIR_ON_DSMLP}/results

# Where the per-user Python venv (transformers/numpy/matplotlib on top of
# the container's own PyTorch) is created. Lives in the home directory so it
# persists across jobs, per DSMLP's package-install guidance.
# Docs: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/environments/customizing-your-environment/
VENV_DIR=${HOME}/.venvs/e-steer

# Where Hugging Face caches the downloaded model weights. Also in the home
# directory so the download only has to happen once.
HF_HOME_DIR=${HOME}/.cache/huggingface
